From bde9b193512ff0b2abaf68d4026c7a1af8418a36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 06:25:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 46/46] mir: don't assume a de-temporary borrow source local is a reference

`MIR_Optimise_DeTemporary_Borrows` looks for locals assigned once from a
`Borrow` rvalue and only used through derefs. `&raw const`/`&raw mut`
(core's `addr_of!`/`addr_of_mut!`) are also lowered to a `Borrow` rvalue,
but the local is a raw pointer, and the multi-use check did
`as_Borrow()` on its type:

    Assertion failed: (m_tag == TAG_Borrow), function as_Borrow,
    file src/hir/type.hpp, line 236.

Hit by libyaml-rs 0.3.0 / unsafe-libyaml 0.2.11 under `-O` (c2rust
output: `let p = addr_of_mut!(x); *p = ..; f(p)`). Raw pointers can be
copied and cast freely, so only shared references get the multi-use
expansion; raw pointer locals keep the existing single-use handling.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mir/optimise.cpp | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mir/optimise.cpp b/src/mir/optimise.cpp
index 66c462ba..05b57ee0 100644
--- a/src/mir/optimise.cpp
+++ b/src/mir/optimise.cpp
@@ -2116,9 +2116,11 @@ bool MIR_Optimise_DeTemporary_Borrows(::MIR::TypeResolve& state, ::MIR::Function
             continue;
         }
         // Keep the complexity down (when not used only once)
-        if( slot.n_deref_read + slot.n_other_read > 1 && fcn.locals[var_idx].data().as_Borrow().type != ::HIR::BorrowType::Shared )
+        // NOTE: `&raw const`/`&raw mut` are also `Borrow` rvalues, but the local is a raw pointer (which can be copied
+        // and cast freely), so only shared references get the multi-use treatment.
+        if( slot.n_deref_read + slot.n_other_read > 1 && !TU_TEST1(fcn.locals[var_idx].data(), Borrow, .type == ::HIR::BorrowType::Shared) )
         {
-            DEBUG(this_var << " - Multi-use non-shared borrow, too complex to do");
+            DEBUG(this_var << " - Multi-use non-shared borrow (or raw pointer), too complex to do");
             continue;
         }
         DEBUG(this_var << " - Borrow of " << src_lv << " at " << slot.set_loc << ", used " << slot.n_deref_read << " times (dropped {" << slot.drop_locs << "})");
